{"abstract":"The VarDial Evaluation Campaign 2025 was organized as part of the twelfth workshop on Natural Language Processing for Similar Languages, Varieties and Dialects (VarDial), colocated with COLING 2025. It consisted of one shared task with three subtasks: intent detection, slot filling and dialect identification for Norwegian dialects. This report presents the results of this shared task. Four participating teams have submitted systems with very high performance (> 97% accuracy) for intent detection, whereas slot detection and dialect identification showed to be much more challenging, with respectively span-F1 scores up to 89%, and weighted dialect F1 scores of 84%.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Scherrer, Yves","van der Goot, Rob","Mæhlum, Petter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828141"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Slot filling","dialect identification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"findings of the vardial evaluation campaign 000000002025 the norsid shared task on norwegian slot intent and dialect identification","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.vardial-1.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828141","identifier":[{"id":"105001918856","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1bb2d88d-6702-4e61-af01-e99bb610ac7a"],"keyword":["Norwegian dialects","VarDial Evaluation Campaign 2025","dialect identification","intent detection","slot filling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-59CBFF417B42672C6EC4CE1029890F53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.vardial-1.1/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.vardial-1.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yves","key":"scherrerpau","last":"Scherrer","name":"Scherrer, Yves","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Petter","key":"mæhlumpau","last":"Mæhlum","name":"Mæhlum, Petter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yves","key":"scherrerpedh","last":"Scherrer","name":"Scherrer, Yves","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tommi","key":"jauhiainenpedh","last":"Jauhiainen","name":"Jauhiainen, Tommi","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nikola","key":"ljubešićpedh","last":"Ljubešić","name":"Ljubešić, Nikola","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Preslav","key":"nakovpedh","last":"Nakov","name":"Nakov, Preslav","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jorg","key":"tiedemannpedh","last":"Tiedemann","name":"Tiedemann, Jorg","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marcos","key":"zampieripedh","last":"Zampieri","name":"Zampieri, Marcos","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"1-8","place":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 12th Workshop on NLP for Similar Languages, Varieties and Dialects"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1bb2d88d-6702-4e61-af01-e99bb610ac7a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Findings of the VarDial Evaluation Campaign 2025: The NorSID Shared Task on Norwegian Slot, Intent and Dialect Identification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828141","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Medical notes contain a wealth of information related to diagnosis, prognosis, and overall patient care that can be used to help physicians make informed decisions. However, like any other data sets consisting of data from diverse demographics, they may be biased toward certain subgroups or subpopulations. Consequently, any bias in the data will be reflected in the output of the machine learning models trained on them. In this paper, we investigate the existence of such biases in Danish medical notes related to three types of blood cancer, with the goal of classifying whether the medical notes indicate severe infection. By employing a hierarchical architecture that combines a sequence model (Transformer and LSTM) with a BERT model to classify long notes, we uncover biases related to demographics and cancer types. Furthermore, we observe performance differences between hospitals. These findings underscore the importance of investigating bias in critical settings such as healthcare and the urgency of monitoring and mitigating it when developing AI-based systems.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Parviz, Mehdi","Agius, Rudi","Niemann, Carsten","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828149"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Electronic Health Records"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bias in danish medical notes infection classification of long texts using transformer and lstm architectures coupled with bert","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.cl4health-1.27","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828149","ids":["itu-50f34068-7a08-480a-8c89-3064cdf6a33b"],"keyword":["Danish medical notes","bias in healthcare AI","clinical natural language processing","electronic health records","hospital-level performance variation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7A033A8574A8D2D0452639165D4021AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.cl4health-1.27","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mehdi","key":"parvizpau","last":"Parviz","name":"Parviz, Mehdi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rudi","key":"agiuspau","last":"Agius","name":"Agius, Rudi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"niemannpau","last":"Niemann","name":"Niemann, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"Van Der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Van Der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sophia","key":"ananiadoupedh","last":"Ananiadou","name":"Ananiadou, Sophia","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dina","key":"demnerfushmanpedh","last":"Demner-Fushman","name":"Demner-Fushman, Dina","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Deepak","key":"guptapedh","last":"Gupta","name":"Gupta, Deepak","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"thompsonpedh","last":"Thompson","name":"Thompson, Paul","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2025.cl4health-1.27","isbn":["9798891762381"],"pages":"316-320","place":"Albuquerque, New Mexico","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Second Workshop on Patient-Oriented Language Processing (CL4Health)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-50f34068-7a08-480a-8c89-3064cdf6a33b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bias in Danish Medical Notes: Infection Classification of Long Texts Using Transformer and LSTM Architectures Coupled with BERT","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828149","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Predicting career trajectories is a complex yet impactful task, offering significant benefits for personalized career counseling, recruitment optimization, and workforce planning. However, effective career path prediction (CPP) modeling faces challenges including highly variable career trajectories, free-text resume data, and limited publicly available benchmark datasets. In this study, we present a comprehensive comparative evaluation of CPP models—linear projection, multilayer perceptron (MLP), LSTM, and large language models (LLMs)—across multiple input settings and two recently introduced public datasets. Our contributions are threefold: (1) we propose novel model variants, including an MLP extension and a standardized LLM approach, (2) we systematically evaluate model performance across input types (titles only vs. title+description, standardized vs. free-text), and (3) we investigate the role of synthetic data and fine-tuning strategies in addressing data scarcity and improving model generalization. Additionally, we provide a detailed qualitative analysis of prediction behaviors across industries, career lengths, and transitions. Our findings establish new baselines, reveal the trade-offs of different modeling strategies, and offer practical insights for deploying CPP systems in real-world settings.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Senger, Elena","Campbell, Yuri","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828157"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich"],"keyword":["Career path prediction","LLM","Labor market","Recommendation","Synthetic data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward more realistic career path prediction evaluation and methods","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdata.2025.1564521","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828157","ids":["itu-640078c3-3cde-48b4-a54f-985b7376a765"],"keyword":["LLM","career path prediction","labor market","recommendation","synthetic data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-09B6503596078F7A465596528060825D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fdata.2025.1564521","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"sengerpau","last":"Senger","name":"Senger, Elena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"campbellpau","last":"Campbell","name":"Campbell, Yuri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","name":"Plank, Barbara","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-640078c3-3cde-48b4-a54f-985b7376a765"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Toward more realistic career path prediction: evaluation and methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828157","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We present SnakModel, a Danish large language model (LLM) based on Llama2-7B, which we continuously pre-train on 13.6B Danish words, and further tune on 3.7M Danish instructions. As best practices for creating LLMs for smaller language communities have yet to be established, we examine the effects of early modeling and training decisions on downstream performance throughout the entire training pipeline, including (1) the creation of a strictly curated corpus of Danish text from diverse sources; (2) the language modeling and instruction-tuning training process itself, including the analysis of intermediate training dynamics, and ablations across different hyperparameters; (3) an evaluation on eight language and culturally-specific tasks. Across these experiments SnakModel achieves the highest overall performance, outperforming multiple contemporary Llama2-7B-based models. By making SnakModel, the majority of our pre-training corpus, and the associated code available under open licenses, we hope to foster further research and development in Danish Natural Language Processing, and establish training guidelines for languages with similar resource constraints.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Müller-Eberstein, Max","Bassignana, Elisa","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S02-087.89-813507"],"event":{"acronym":"NODALIDA","title":"Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Large Language Model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"snakmodel lessons learned from training an open danish large language model","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.80/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.89-813507","ids":["aau-f723cc80-f5e3-4c09-996e-b1ba16b9c7f2","itu-bb98c006-6693-41e0-b20c-84f6825ba953"],"keyword":["Danish language model","large language model","low-resource language NLP","open-source NLP","pre-training instruction-tuning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-938A605423C4806B7CA2E68B0C70B68D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.80/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Northern European Association for Language Technology","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 25th Nordic Conference on Computational Lingustics and 11th Baltic Conference on Human Language Technologies : NoDaLiDa/Baltic-HLT 2025"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f723cc80-f5e3-4c09-996e-b1ba16b9c7f2","itu-bb98c006-6693-41e0-b20c-84f6825ba953"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SnakModel : Lessons Learned from Training an Open Danish Large Language Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.89-813507","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have seen widespread societal adoption. However, while they are able to interact with users in languages beyond English, they have been shown to lack cultural awareness, providing anglocentric or inappropriate responses for underrepresented language communities. To investigate this gap and disentangle linguistic versus cultural proficiency, we conduct the first cultural evaluation study for the mid-resource language of Danish, in which native speakers prompt different models to solve tasks requiring cultural awareness. Our analysis of the resulting 1,038 interactions from 63 demographically diverse participants highlights open challenges to cultural adaptation: Particularly, how currently employed automatically translated data are insufficient to train or measure cultural adaptation, and how training on native-speaker data can more than double response acceptance rates. We release our study data as DaKultur - the first native Danish cultural awareness dataset.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Müller-Eberstein, Max","Zhang, Mike","Bassignana, Elisa","Brunsgaard Trolle, Peter","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S02-091.89-813317"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cultural Awareness","Danish language","Large Language Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dakultur evaluating the cultural awareness of language models for danish with native speakers","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.c3nlp-1.5/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.89-813317","ids":["aau-285c9042-fdc3-47f3-b49c-80a84514b36d","itu-39488485-b9dc-4aab-b098-1a00f4ad5114"],"keyword":["Cultural Awareness","DaKultur Dataset","Danish Language","Large Language Models","Native-Speaker Data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-CC65833422460DE272D3DF96AF29DBBB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.c3nlp-1.5/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"brunsgaardtrollepau","last":"Brunsgaard Trolle","name":"Brunsgaard Trolle, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brunsgaard","key":"trollepau","last":"Trolle","locid":"d21db1f2-9a89-4611-8077-e06e89985faa","name":"Trolle, Peter Brunsgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"3rd Workshop on Cross-Cultural Considerations in NLP (C3NLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-285c9042-fdc3-47f3-b49c-80a84514b36d","itu-39488485-b9dc-4aab-b098-1a00f4ad5114"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DaKultur : Evaluating the Cultural Awareness of Language Models for Danish with Native Speakers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.89-813317","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Language typology databases enhance multilingual Natural Language Processing (NLP) by improving model adaptability to diverse linguistic structures. The widely-used lang2vec toolkit integrates several such databases, but its coverage remains limited at 28.9%. Previous work on automatically increasing coverage predicts missing values based on features from other languages or focuses on single features; we propose to use textual data for better-informed feature prediction. To this end, we introduce a multi-lingual Part-of-Speech (POS) tagger, achieving over 70% accuracy across 1,749 languages, and experiment with external statistical features and a variety of machine learning algorithms. We also introduce a more realistic evaluation setup, focusing on likely to be missing typology features, and show that our approach outperforms previous work in both setups.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Amirzadeh, Hamidreza","Jafari, Sadegh","Harju, Anika","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828158"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Iran University of Science and Technology","Sharif University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data000000000002lang000000000002vec data driven typological features completion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-main.435.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828158","identifier":[{"id":"85218490732","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-64bc135f-7034-4191-b5c6-975ba3c36db0"],"keyword":["Linguistic typology databases","Multilingual POS tagging","Multilingual natural language processing","Typology coverage evaluation","Typology feature prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-410AAB77701E318BB920DF3EE7E5029F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-main.435/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-main.435.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ir","key":"sharif university of technology","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Sharif University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ir","key":"iran university of science and technology","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Iran University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hamidreza","key":"amirzadehpau","last":"Amirzadeh","name":"Amirzadeh, Hamidreza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sadegh","key":"jafaripau","last":"Jafari","name":"Jafari, Sadegh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anika","key":"harjupau","last":"Harju","name":"Harju, Anika","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Owen","key":"rambowpedh","last":"Rambow","name":"Rambow, Owen","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Leo","key":"wannerpedh","last":"Wanner","name":"Wanner, Leo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marianna","key":"apidianakipedh","last":"Apidianaki","name":"Apidianaki, Marianna","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Hend","key":"alkhalifapedh","last":"Al-Khalifa","name":"Al-Khalifa, Hend","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Barbara Di","key":"eugeniopedh","last":"Eugenio","name":"Eugenio, Barbara Di","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Steven","key":"schockaertpedh","last":"Schockaert","name":"Schockaert, Steven","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"6520-6529","place":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 31st International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-64bc135f-7034-4191-b5c6-975ba3c36db0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"data2lang2vec: Data Driven Typological Features Completion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828158","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Automatic language identification is a core problem of many Natural LanguageProcessing (NLP) pipelines. A wide variety of architectures and benchmarks havebeen proposed with often near-perfect performance. Although previousstudies have focused on certain challenging setups (i.e. cross-domain, shortinputs), a systematic comparison is missing. We propose a benchmark that allows us to test for the effect of input size, training data size, domain, number oflanguages, scripts, and language families on performance. We evaluatefive popular models on this benchmark and identify which open challengesremain for this task as well as which architectures achieve robust performance. Wefind that cross-domain setups are the most challenging (although arguably mostrelevant), and that number of languages, variety in scripts, and variety inlanguage families have only a small impact on performance. We also contributepractical takeaways: training with 1,000 instances per language and a maximuminput length of 100 characters is enough for robust language identification.Based on our findings, we train an accurate (94.41{\\%}) multi-domain languageidentification model on 2,034 languages, for which we also provide an analysisof the remaining errors.","author_count":5,"contributors":["van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828166"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross Domain Evaluation","Language identification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identifying open challenges in language identification","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.acl-long.891","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828166","ids":["itu-8d3e621c-1479-452e-9e9b-6d8d18cb25ce"],"keyword":["Cross-domain evaluation","Language identification","Multilingual benchmarks","Script variation and language families","Training data efficiency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6748FA27D5B014F32DA00BFBAB02AA25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.acl-long.891","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob Van Der","key":"gootpau","last":"Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Goot, Rob Van Der","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wanxiang","key":"chepedh","last":"Che","name":"Che, Wanxiang","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joyce","key":"nabendepedh","last":"Nabende","name":"Nabende, Joyce","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ekaterina","key":"shutovapedh","last":"Shutova","name":"Shutova, Ekaterina","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohammad Taher","key":"pilehvarpedh","last":"Pilehvar","name":"Pilehvar, Mohammad Taher","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2025.acl-long.891","isbn":["9798891762510"],"pages":"18207-18227","place":"Vienna, Austria","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 1: Long Papers)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8d3e621c-1479-452e-9e9b-6d8d18cb25ce"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Identifying Open Challenges in Language Identification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828166","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Matching job titles is a highly relevant task in the computational job market domain, as it improves e.g., automatic candidate matching, career path prediction, and job market analysis. Furthermore, aligning job titles to job skills can be considered an extension to this task, with similar relevance for the same downstream tasks. In this report, we outline NLPnorth's submission to TalentCLEF 2025, which includes both of these tasks: Multilingual Job Title Matching, and Job Title-Based Skill Prediction. For both tasks we compare (fine-tuned) classification-based, (fine-tuned) contrastive-based, and prompting methods. We observe that for Task A, our prompting approach performs best with an average of 0.492 mean average precision (MAP) on test data, averaged over English, Spanish, and German. For Task B, we obtain an MAP of 0.290 on test data with our fine-tuned classification-based approach. Additionally, we made use of extra data by pulling all the language-specific titles and corresponding \\emph{descriptions} from ESCO for each job and skill. Overall, we find that the largest multilingual language models perform best for both tasks. Per the provisional results and only counting the unique teams, the ranking on Task A is 5$^{\\text{th}}$/20 and for Task B 3$^{\\text{rd}}$/14.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-823354"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cs CL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nlpnorth talentclef 000000002025 comparing discriminative contrastive and prompt based methods for job title and skill matching","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/790917596/2506.19058v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-823354","ids":["aau-3714efde-cbf9-4ff7-88ae-faf2620f499a"],"keyword":["cs.CL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-76B8B8CC0C3F18FC266BCC4A0638ED76"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/790917596/2506.19058v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","name":"van der Goot, Rob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3714efde-cbf9-4ff7-88ae-faf2620f499a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"NLPnorth @ TalentCLEF 2025 : Comparing Discriminative, Contrastive, and Prompt-Based Methods for Job Title and Skill Matching","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-823354","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Traditional language model compression techniques, like knowledge distillation, require a fixed architecture, limiting flexibility, while structured pruning methods often fail to preserve performance. This paper introduces Iterative Structured Knowledge Distillation (ISKD), which integrates knowledge distillation and structured pruning by progressively replacing transformer blocks with smaller, efficient versions during training. This study validates ISKD on two transformer-based language models: GPT-2 and Phi-1. ISKD outperforms L1 pruning and achieves similar performance to knowledge distillation while offering greater flexibility. ISKD reduces model parameters - 30.68% for GPT-2 and 30.16% for Phi-1 - while maintaining at least four-fifths of performance on both language modeling and commonsense reasoning tasks. These findings suggest that this method offers a promising balance between model efficiency and accuracy.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Musaeus, Malthe Have","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828140"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Structured pruning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"iterative structured knowledge distillation optimizing language models through layer by layer distillation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-main.440.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828140","identifier":[{"id":"85218499447","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-16af6681-d76f-4a8f-8ee8-d9f111f6c0fe"],"keyword":["Iterative Structured Knowledge Distillation","Language model compression","Parameter-efficient NLP","Structured pruning","Transformer block replacement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9D290F7B511F9EE5A7C7D4952135A09A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-main.440.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Malthe Have","key":"musaeuspau","last":"Musaeus","name":"Musaeus, Malthe Have","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Owen","key":"rambowpedh","last":"Rambow","name":"Rambow, Owen","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Leo","key":"wannerpedh","last":"Wanner","name":"Wanner, Leo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marianna","key":"apidianakipedh","last":"Apidianaki","name":"Apidianaki, Marianna","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Hend","key":"alkhalifapedh","last":"Al-Khalifa","name":"Al-Khalifa, Hend","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Barbara Di","key":"eugeniopedh","last":"Eugenio","name":"Eugenio, Barbara Di","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Steven","key":"schockaertpedh","last":"Schockaert","name":"Schockaert, Steven","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"6601-6606","place":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 31st International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-16af6681-d76f-4a8f-8ee8-d9f111f6c0fe"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Iterative Structured Knowledge Distillation: Optimizing Language Models Through Layer-by-Layer Distillation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828140","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The best performing transformer-based language models use subword tokenization techniques, such as Byte-Pair-Encoding (BPE). However, these approaches often overlook linguistic principles, such as morphological segmentation, which we believe is fundamental for understanding language-specific word structure. In this study, we leverage an annotated Danish morphological dataset to train a semisupervised model for morphological segmentation, enabling the development of tokenizers optimized for Danish morphology. We evaluate four distinct tokenizers, including two custom morphological tokenizers, by analyzing their performance in morphologically segmenting Danish words. Additionally, we train two generative transformer models, \\textit{CerebrasGPT-111M} and \\textit{LLaMA-3.2 1B}, using these tokenizers and evaluate their downstream performance. Our findings reveal that our custom-developed tokenizers substantially enhance morphological segmentation, achieving an F1 score of 58.84, compared to 39.28 achieved by a Danish BPE tokenizer. In downstream tasks, models trained with our morphological tokenizers outperform those using BPE tokenizers across different evaluation metrics. These results highlight that incorporating Danish morphological segmentation strategies into tokenizers leads to improved performance in generative transformer models on Danish language","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kildeberg, Mikkel Wildner","Schledermann, Emil Allerslev","Larsen, Nicolaj","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828173"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Morphological segmentation","Semisupervised learning","Transformer based language models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from smør re brød to subwords training llms on danish one morpheme at a time","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.01540","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828173","ids":["itu-aedf4cf5-f14d-47fe-a99b-b0dcfc0d8fa2"],"keyword":["Danish language morphology","Morphological segmentation","Semisupervised learning","Tokenization methods","Transformer-based language models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-38A929CD33FCC344C5CDCF479DA2391F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.01540","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Wildner","key":"kildebergpau","last":"Kildeberg","name":"Kildeberg, Mikkel Wildner","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Allerslev","key":"schledermannpau","last":"Schledermann","name":"Schledermann, Emil Allerslev","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolaj","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Nicolaj","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob van der","key":"gootpau","last":"Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Goot, Rob van der","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-aedf4cf5-f14d-47fe-a99b-b0dcfc0d8fa2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From Smør-re-brød to Subwords: Training LLMs on Danish, One Morpheme at a Time","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828173","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Symmetric patterns are found in the orderly arrangements of natural structures, from proteins to the symmetry in animals’ bodies. Symmetric structures are more stable and easier to describe and compress, which is why they may have been preferred as building blocks in natural selection. The idea that natural languages undergo an evolutionary process akin to the evolution of species has been pervasive in the study of language. This process might result in symmetric patterns as in other natural structures, but the notion of symmetry is rarely associated with the study of natural language. In this study, we look for symmetric patterns in text data, considering the length of subword units under a range of possible subword analyses. We study the length of subword units in 32 languages and discover that the splits of long words tend to be symmetric regardless of the segmentation method and that some automatic methods give symmetric splits at all word lengths. These results include natural language in the set of phenomena that can be described in terms of symmetry, opening a new research avenue for the empirical study of text data as a structure comparable to various other structures in the natural world.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pelloni, Olga","van der Goot, Rob","Ranacher, Peter","Vulic, Ivan","Samardzic, Tanja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828156"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge","University of Zurich"],"keyword":["Natural Language","Symmetry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subword symmetry in natural languages","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.250295","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828156","identifier":[{"id":"105013836702","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5e82f36a-bb35-46b2-b501-238a8c003b3d"],"keyword":["Natural language","Subword segmentation","Symmetry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6D72AB17710A11BDFFB4D2BB3EC75703"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://royalsocietypublishing.org/doi/epdf/10.1098/rsos.250295","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.250295","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"university of zurich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Zurich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olga","key":"pellonipau","last":"Pelloni","name":"Pelloni, Olga","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"ranacherpau","last":"Ranacher","name":"Ranacher, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan","key":"vulicpau","last":"Vulic","name":"Vulic, Ivan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tanja","key":"samardzicpau","last":"Samardzic","name":"Samardzic, Tanja","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1098/rsos.250295","issn":["20545703"],"issue":"8","journal":"Royal Society Open Science","pages":"1-29","status":"p","title":"Royal Society Open Science","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013836702"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5e82f36a-bb35-46b2-b501-238a8c003b3d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Subword symmetry in natural languages","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828156","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"author_count":10,"contributors":["Harju, Anika","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828142"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to age bert well continuous training for historical language adaptation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.loreslm-1.21.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828142","identifier":[{"id":"105000195929","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1e22a358-282a-42d9-a0c5-4a4d1115f247"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6B2531FFB6805CD260D98F893EEFD3BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.loreslm-1.21.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.loreslm-1.21/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anika","key":"harjupau","last":"Harju","name":"Harju, Anika","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hansi","key":"hettiarachchipedh","last":"Hettiarachchi","name":"Hettiarachchi, Hansi","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tharindu","key":"ranasinghepedh","last":"Ranasinghe","name":"Ranasinghe, Tharindu","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"raysonpedh","last":"Rayson","name":"Rayson, Paul","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ruslan","key":"mitkovpedh","last":"Mitkov","name":"Mitkov, Ruslan","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohamed","key":"gaberpedh","last":"Gaber","name":"Gaber, Mohamed","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Damith","key":"premasiripedh","last":"Premasiri","name":"Premasiri, Damith","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Fiona Anting","key":"tanpedh","last":"Tan","name":"Tan, Fiona Anting","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lasitha","key":"uyangodagepedh","last":"Uyangodage","name":"Uyangodage, Lasitha","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"258-267","place":"Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the First Workshop on Language Models for Low-Resource Languages"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1e22a358-282a-42d9-a0c5-4a4d1115f247"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to age BERT Well: Continuous Training for Historical Language Adaptation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828142","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Current language models (LMs) mostly exploit subwords as input units based on statistical co-occurrences of characters. Adjacently, previous work has shown that modeling morphemes can aid performance for Natural Language Processing (NLP) models. However, morphemes are challenging to obtain as there is no annotated data in most languages. In this work, we release a wide-coverage Danish morphological segmentation evaluation set. We evaluate a wide variety of unsupervised token segmenters and evaluate the downstream effect of using morphemes as input units for transformer-based LMs. Our results show that popular subword algorithms perform poorly on this task, scoring at most an $F_1$ of 44.8 compared to 58.6 for an unsupervised morphological segmented (Morfessor). Furthermore, we confirm that the more closely our tokenizer resembles morphemes, the higher the performance of LMs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["van der Goot, Rob","Jensen, Anette","Allerslev Schledermann, Emil","Wildner Kildeberg, Mikkel","Larsen, Nicolaj","Zhang, Mike","Bassignana, Elisa"],"cuid":["S02-083.61-822464"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Danish language processing","Morphological segmentation","Transformer based language models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"morsed morphological segmentation of danish and its effect on language modeling","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.23.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.61-822464","ids":["aau-cdd51d4a-0153-4cd6-b5ca-2c7f2c97e306","itu-a4555d83-5f29-4b04-b0c3-13151f26d4c8"],"keyword":["Danish language processing","Morpheme-based input representations","Morphological segmentation","Transformer-based language models","Unsupervised token segmentation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-321607212045F25CBC149346C9489375"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.23/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.23.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob van der","key":"gootpau","last":"Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Goot, Rob van der","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Anette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Allerslev","key":"schledermannpau","last":"Schledermann","name":"Schledermann, Emil Allerslev","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Wildner","key":"kildebergpau","last":"Kildeberg","name":"Kildeberg, Mikkel Wildner","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolaj","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Nicolaj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Richard","key":"johanssonpedh","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Richard","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sara","key":"stymnepedh","last":"Stymne","name":"Stymne, Sara","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789908531090"],"pages":"223-229","place":"Tallinn, Estonia","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Joint 25th Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics and 11th Baltic Conference on Human Language Technologies (NoDaLiDa/Baltic-HLT 2025)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cdd51d4a-0153-4cd6-b5ca-2c7f2c97e306","itu-a4555d83-5f29-4b04-b0c3-13151f26d4c8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MorSeD : Morphological Segmentation of Danish and its Effect on Language Modeling","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.61-822464","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Accurate career path prediction can support many stakeholders, like job seekers, recruiters, HR, and project managers. However, publicly available data and tools for career path prediction are scarce. In this work, we introduce Karrierewege, a comprehensive, publicly available dataset containing over 500k career paths, significantly surpassing the size of previously available datasets. We link the dataset to the ESCO taxonomy to offer a valuable resource for predicting career trajectories. To tackle the problem of free-text inputs typically found in resumes, we enhance it by synthesizing job titles and descriptions resulting in Karrierewege+. This allows for accurate predictions from unstructured data, closely aligning with practical application challenges. We benchmark existing state-of-the-art (SOTA) models on our dataset and a previous benchmark and see increased performance and robustness by synthesizing the data for the free-text use cases.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Senger, Elena","Campbell, Yuri","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828138"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fraunhofer Center for International Management and Knowledge Economics (IMW)","MaiNLP research lab"],"keyword":["Career path prediction","ESCO Taxonomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"karrierewege a large scale career path prediction dataset","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-industry.46.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828138","identifier":[{"id":"105000138631","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-07ed9e70-3571-4a3b-b403-e6d7fb963e3b"],"keyword":["Career path prediction","Career trajectories dataset","ESCO taxonomy","Resume NLP","Synthetic resume data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-64C5D186530F15046DEC6CAD42F33610"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-industry.46.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.coling-industry.46/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"mainlp research lab","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"MaiNLP research lab","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer center for international management and knowledge economics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Center for International Management and Knowledge Economics (IMW)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"sengerpau","last":"Senger","name":"Senger, Elena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"campbellpau","last":"Campbell","name":"Campbell, Yuri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecod