EGE: A large scale Career Path Prediction Dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828138","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The study of generalization in Language Models (LMs) requires controlled experiments that can precisely measure complex linguistic variations between training and testing datasets. We introduce DECAF, a framework that enables the analysis and filtering of linguistically-annotated datasets down to the character level. Rather than creating new resources for each experiment, DECAF starts from datasets with existing linguistic annotations, and leverages them to analyze, filter, and generate highly controlled and reproducible experimental settings targeting specific research questions. We demonstrate DECAF’s functionality by adding 28 morphosyntactic annotation layers to the 115M-word BabyLM corpus and indexing the resulting 1.1B annotations to analyze its internal domain variance, and to create a controlled training data curriculum for a small-scale gender bias study. We release DECAF as an open-source Python library, along with the parsed and indexed version of BabyLM, as resources for future generalization research.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Müller-Eberstein, Max","van der Goot, Rob","Rogers, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828155"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"decaf a dynamically extensible corpus analysis framework","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.acl-demo.34","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828155","ids":["itu-5cbe7861-e985-4e15-a68d-b3761946b950"],"keyword":["bias analysis in NLP","dataset curation and filtering","language model generalization","linguistic annotations","reproducible experimentation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FF89B6363624FE6AEF9BA899708E1312"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.acl-demo.34","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob Van Der","key":"gootpau","last":"Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Goot, Rob Van Der","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pushkar","key":"mishrapedh","last":"Mishra","name":"Mishra, Pushkar","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Smaranda","key":"muresanpedh","last":"Muresan","name":"Muresan, Smaranda","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tao","key":"yupedh","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Tao","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2025.acl-demo.34","isbn":["9798891762534"],"pages":"351-362","place":"Vienna, Austria","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (Volume 3: System Demonstrations)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5cbe7861-e985-4e15-a68d-b3761946b950"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DECAF: A Dynamically Extensible Corpus Analysis Framework","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828155","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Large language models have emerged as a useful technology for job matching, for both candidates and employers. Job matching is often based on a particular geographic location, such as a city or region. However, LMs have known biases, commonly derived from their training data. In this work, we aim to quantify the metropolitan size bias encoded within large language models, evaluating zero-shot salary, employer presence, and commute duration predictions in 384 of the United States' metropolitan regions. Across all benchmarks, we observe correlations between metropolitan population and the accuracy of predictions, with the smallest 10 metropolitan regions showing upwards of 300% worse benchmark performance than the largest 10.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Campanella, Charlie","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776367"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Indeed"],"keyword":["Job matching","Large Language Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"big city bias evaluating the impact of metropolitan size on computational job market abilities of language models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776367","identifier":[{"id":"85190288985","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0a3bb1de-4f1e-463f-8bfd-39ecbaca8b46"],"keyword":["Large language models","job matching","metropolitan region benchmarks","metropolitan size bias","zero-shot salary prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-02BBEFA6DFAE6CF0A26444B314C3EBA3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.6","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"indeed","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Indeed","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlie","key":"campanellapau","last":"Campanella","name":"Campanella, Charlie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Estevam","key":"hruschkapedh","last":"Hruschka","name":"Hruschka, Estevam","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thom","key":"lakepedh","last":"Lake","name":"Lake, Thom","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Naoki","key":"otanipedh","last":"Otani","name":"Otani, Naoki","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tom","key":"mitchellpedh","last":"Mitchell","name":"Mitchell, Tom","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"73-77","place":"St. Julian's, Malta","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the First Workshop on Natural Language Processing for Human Resources (NLP4HR 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0a3bb1de-4f1e-463f-8bfd-39ecbaca8b46"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Big City Bias: Evaluating the Impact of Metropolitan Size on Computational Job Market Abilities of Language Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776367","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Digital assistants perform well in high-resource languages like English, where tasks like slot and intent detection (SID) are well-supported. Many recent SID datasets start including multiple language varieties. However, it is unclear how realistic these translated datasets are. Therefore, we extend one such dataset, namely xSID-0.4, to include two underrepresented languages: Bavarian, a German dialect, and Lithuanian, a Baltic language. Both language variants have limited speaker populations and are often not included in multilingual projects. In addition to translations we provide ``natural'' queries to digital assistants generated by native speakers. We further include utterances from another dataset for Bavarian to build the richest SID dataset available today for a low-resource dialect without standard orthography. We then set out to evaluate models trained on English in a zero-shot scenario on our target language variants. Our evaluation reveals that translated data can produce overly optimistic scores. However, the error patterns in translated and natural datasets are highly similar. Cross-dataset experiments demonstrate that data collection methods influence performance, with scores lower than those achieved with single-dataset translations. This work contributes to enhancing SID datasets for underrepresented languages, yielding NaLiBaSID, a new evaluation dataset for Bavarian and Lithuanian.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Winkler, Miriam","Juozapaityte, Virginija","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776416"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich"],"keyword":["Zero shot learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"slot and intent detection resources for bavarian and lithuanian assessing translations vs natural queries to digital assistants","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.1297","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776416","identifier":[{"id":"85195904749","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-78e84191-d8f4-46cd-84d0-1d05c08bceb9"],"keyword":["Dataset creation and cross-dataset evaluation for SID","Low-resource languages and dialects","Multilingual natural language understanding","Slot filling and intent detection (SID)","Zero-shot learning"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C14CCA0E1340D738BF0EECDDF503D7C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.1297","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miriam","key":"winklerpau","last":"Winkler","name":"Winkler, Miriam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Virginija","key":"juozapaitytepau","last":"Juozapaityte","name":"Juozapaityte, Virginija","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicoletta","key":"calzolaripedh","last":"Calzolari","name":"Calzolari, Nicoletta","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Min-Yen","key":"kanpedh","last":"Kan","name":"Kan, Min-Yen","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Veronique","key":"hostepedh","last":"Hoste","name":"Hoste, Veronique","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alessandro","key":"lencipedh","last":"Lenci","name":"Lenci, Alessandro","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sakriani","key":"saktipedh","last":"Sakti","name":"Sakti, Sakriani","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nianwen","key":"xuepedh","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Nianwen","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"14898-14915","place":"Torino, Italia","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Joint International Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC-COLING 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-78e84191-d8f4-46cd-84d0-1d05c08bceb9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Slot and Intent Detection Resources for Bavarian and Lithuanian: Assessing Translations vs Natural Queries to Digital Assistants","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776416","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Annotation tools are the starting point for creating Natural Language Processing (NLP) datasets. There is a wide variety of tools available; setting up these tools is however a hindrance. We propose Eevee, an annotation tool focused on simplicity, efficiency, and ease of use. It can run directly in the browser (no setup required) and uses tab-separated files (as opposed to character offsets or task-specific formats) for annotation. It allows for annotation of multiple tasks on a single dataset and supports four task-types: sequence labeling, span labeling, text classification and seq2seq.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sorensen, Axel","Peng, Siyao","Plank, Barbara","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776398"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Munich Center for Machine Learning (MCML)"],"keyword":["Annotation tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eevee an easy annotation tool for natural language processing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85188684871","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776398","identifier":[{"id":"85188684871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4e17ab98-6c05-4726-ab59-a06e70afc823"],"keyword":["annotation tools","browser-based annotation","multi-task annotation","natural language processing datasets","tab-separated data format"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4742ACE9D4E795FA914371E2F8C4F69E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"munich center for machine learning","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Munich Center for Machine Learning (MCML)","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","name":"Sorensen, Axel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyao","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Siyao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"Van Der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Van Der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sophie","key":"henningpedh","last":"Henning","name":"Henning, Sophie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manfred","key":"stedepedh","last":"Stede","name":"Stede, Manfred","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"216-221","place":"St. Julians, Malta","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of The 18th Linguistic Annotation Workshop (LAW-XVIII)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4e17ab98-6c05-4726-ab59-a06e70afc823"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EEVEE: An Easy Annotation Tool for Natural Language Processing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776398","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Textual domain is a crucial property within the Natural Language Processing (NLP) community due to its effects on downstream model performance. The concept itself is, however, loosely defined and, in practice, refers to any non-typological property, such as genre, topic, medium or style of a document. We investigate the core notion of domains via human proficiency in identifying related intrinsic textual properties, specifically the concepts of genre (communicative purpose) and topic (subject matter). We publish our annotations in TGeGUM: A collection of 9.1k sentences from the GUM dataset (Zeldes, 2017) with single sentence and larger context (i.e., prose) annotations for one of 11 genres (source type), and its topic/subtopic as per the Dewey Decimal library classification system (Dewey, 1979), consisting of 10/100 hierarchical topics of increased granularity. Each instance is annotated by three annotators, for a total of 32.7k annotations, allowing us to examine the level of human disagreement and the relative difficulty of each annotation task. With a Fleiss' kappa of at most 0.53 on the sentence level and 0.66 at the prose level, it is evident that despite the ubiquity of domains in NLP, there is little human consensus on how to define them. By training classifiers to perform the same task, we find that this uncertainty also extends to NLP models.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria","Müller-Eberstein, Max","Bassignana, Elisa","Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-744102"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-25","place":"Hybrid, Torino, it","start":"2024-05-20","title":"Joint 30th International Conference on Computational Linguistics and 14th International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation, LREC-COLING 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DOMAIN","Genre","Topic","multi annotation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Pioneer Centre for Artificial Intelligence"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can humans identify domains","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85195922379","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-744102","identifier":[{"id":"85195922379","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-40900102-8377-4ff0-8927-c83e7dd4e900"],"keyword":["domain","genre","multi-annotation","topic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-EE1AEFD118029740AC79C5E8ED86A4C4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Pioneer Centre for Artificial Intelligence"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University (AAU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","name":"Barrett, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalie Brogaard","key":"paulipau","last":"Pauli","locid":"6619aaa8-f1c0-4a8a-8d04-23bcf5b0c7ba","name":"Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Mike","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","name":"van der Goot, Rob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicoletta","key":"calzolaripedh","last":"Calzolari","name":"Calzolari, Nicoletta","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Min-Yen","key":"kanpedh","last":"Kan","name":"Kan, Min-Yen","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Veronique","key":"hostepedh","last":"Hoste","name":"Hoste, Veronique","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alessandro","key":"lencipedh","last":"Lenci","name":"Lenci, Alessandro","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sakriani","key":"saktipedh","last":"Sakti","name":"Sakti, Sakriani","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nianwen","key":"xuepedh","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Nianwen","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9782493814104"],"pages":"2745-2765","publisher":"European Language Resources Association (ELRA)","series":"LREC-COLING - Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2024 Joint International Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation, LREC-COLING 2024 - Main Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195922379"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-40900102-8377-4ff0-8927-c83e7dd4e900"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Can Humans Identify Domains?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-744102","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Current language models require a lot of training data to obtain high performance. For Relation Classification (RC), many datasets are domain-specific, so combining datasets to obtain better performance is non-trivial. We explore a multi-domain training setup for RC, and attempt to improve performance by encoding domain information. Our proposed models improve > 2 Macro-F1 against the baseline setup, and our analysis reveals that not all the labels benefit the same: The classes which occupy a similar space across domains (i.e., their interpretation is close across them, for example “physical”) benefit the least, while domain-dependent relations (e.g., “part-of”) improve the most when encoding domain information.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bassignana, Elisa","Unmack Gascou, Viggo","Nøhr Laustsen, Frida","Kristensen, Gustav","Haahr Petersen, Marie","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747225"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DOMAIN","Multi domain training","Relation Classification","Robustness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to encode domain information in relation classification","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.728.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747225","identifier":[{"id":"85195940749","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4a4cff0a-a185-4211-9e3d-907605af2508"],"keyword":["Domain","Multi-domain training","Relation Classification","Robustness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-97A3E9F53EED0AA028ED91388E49D33E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.728.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Viggo","key":"unmackgascoupau","last":"Unmack Gascou","name":"Unmack Gascou, Viggo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frida","key":"nøhrlaustsenpau","last":"Nøhr Laustsen","name":"Nøhr Laustsen, Frida","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gustav","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Gustav","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"haahrpetersenpau","last":"Haahr Petersen","name":"Haahr Petersen, Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"8301-8306","publisher":"European Language Resources Association","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Joint International Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC-COLING 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4a4cff0a-a185-4211-9e3d-907605af2508"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to Encode Domain Information in Relation Classification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747225","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Many Natural Language Processing (NLP) tasks are labeled on the token level, forthese tasks, the first step is to identify the tokens (tokenization). Becausethis step is often considered to be a solved problem, gold tokenization iscommonly assumed. In this paper, we propose an efficient method fortokenization with subword-based language models, and reflect on the status ofperformance on the tokenization task by evaluating on 122 languages in 20different scripts. We show that our proposed model performs on par with thestate-of-the-art, and that tokenization performance is mainly dependent on theamount and consistency of annotated data. We conclude that besidesinconsistencies in the data and exceptional cases the task can be consideredsolved for Latin languages for in-dataset settings (textgreater99.5 F1). However,performance is 0.75 F1 point lower on average for datasets in other scripts andperformance deteriorates in cross-dataset setups.","author_count":3,"contributors":["van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776452"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Tokenization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"where are we still split on tokenization","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776452","identifier":[{"id":"85188745092","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-debca73d-1cbc-468c-b15f-666b74d5c158"],"keyword":["annotation consistency","cross-dataset generalization","cross-script multilingual evaluation","subword-based language models","tokenization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4090761C8A9FBE77119ED7F451FAFD6D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yvette","key":"grahampedh","last":"Graham","name":"Graham, Yvette","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthew","key":"purverpedh","last":"Purver","name":"Purver, Matthew","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"118-137","place":"St. Julian's, Malta","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: EACL 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-debca73d-1cbc-468c-b15f-666b74d5c158"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Where are we Still Split on Tokenization?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776452","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Textual domain is a crucial property within the Natural Language Processing (NLP) community due to its effects on downstream model performance. The concept itself is, however, loosely defined and, in practice, refers to any non-typological property, such as genre, topic, medium or style of a document. We investigate the core notion of domains via the human proficiency in identifying related intrinsic textual properties, specifically the concepts of genre (communicative purpose) and topic (subject matter), and publish our annotations in TGeGUM: A collection of 9.1k sentences from the GUM dataset (Zeldes, 2017) with single sentence and larger context (i.e., prose) annotations for one of 11 genres (source type), and its topic/subtopic as per the Dewey Decimal library classification system (Dewey, 1979), consisting of 10/100 hierarchical topics of increased granularity. Each instance is annotated by three annotators, for a total of 32.7k annotations, allowing us to examine the level of human disagreement and the relative difficulty of each annotation task. With a Fleiss’ kappa of at most 0.53 on the sentence level and 0.66 at the prose level, it is evident that despite the ubiquity of domains in NLP, there is actually little human consensus on how to define them. By training classifiers to perform the same task, we find that this uncertainty also extends to NLP models.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria","Müller-Eberstein, Max","Bassignana, Elisa","Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S02-094.66-741398"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-25","place":"Torino, it","start":"2024-05-20","title":"LREC-COLING 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Silo AI"],"keyword":["DOMAIN","Genre","Topic","multi annotation"],"level":